  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Hub API server",
      "items": [
        "Holds the SpokeCluster objects you create. It is the one place the CLI and the controller agree on.",
        "Every write goes through the webhooks first, so a bad spec never reaches the controller.",
        "The controller writes its four conditions back here, and that is what vela spokes reads."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Admission webhooks",
      "items": [
        "Fill in the defaults and reject specs the connect path cannot honour.",
        "A kubeconfig Secret in another namespace is refused here rather than failing later in the loop.",
        "infraProvisioning, blueprintRef and rolloutStrategyRef are Phase 2 fields, so they are rejected while mode is connect."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "SpokeCluster reconciler",
      "items": [
        "The loop that does the work: get a credential, write the gateway Secret, probe the spoke, record what it found.",
        "It stops at the first failure and says so in a condition, so a broken credential never reports Connected.",
        "It asks to be woken after the probe interval, or sooner when the credential expires first."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Credential providers",
      "items": [
        "Turn whatever the spec declared into one usable set of facts: an endpoint, a CA, and either a token or a client certificate.",
        "The kubeconfig provider reads a Secret. The AWS provider assumes the per-cluster role, describes the EKS cluster, and presigns a token.",
        "The azure and gcp arms pass schema validation but no provider builds them, so those spokes never connect."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Credential cache",
      "items": [
        "Keeps the last materialized credential in memory so the controller does not call AWS on every probe.",
        "An entry is dropped when the spec generation changes, when it nears its refresh deadline, or when the spoke answers 401.",
        "It lives in the process, so a controller restart re-derives every credential."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Gateway Secret",
      "items": [
        "The handoff point. The controller writes the connection details into vela-system and cluster-gateway reads them by Secret name.",
        "An owner annotation records which SpokeCluster wrote it, so a Secret from a manual vela cluster join is left alone.",
        "Deleting the SpokeCluster removes this Secret under detach and keeps it under orphan."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "cluster-gateway and the spoke",
      "items": [
        "cluster-gateway proxies hub requests to the spoke API server, so the controller never dials the spoke itself.",
        "The probe is a plain healthz call through that proxy; a pass also reads the version and nodes for the inventory.",
        "TLS is verified against the endpoint host, so a kubeconfig needing a different server name is refused before any write."
      ]
    }
  ]
